 {
  "op": "set",
  "collection": "lessons",
  "doc_id": "02",
  "data": {
   "title": "Reading the bits",
   "kind": "lesson",
   "script": null,
   "pass": "You can now read any 8-bit two's complement number.",
   "html": "<h2>Your guess</h2>\n<p>Last time: which number is <code>10000011</code>? You said <b>c) -3</b>. It is <b>b) -125</b>.</p>\n<h2>The idea</h2>\n<p>Unsigned, the 8 bits weigh 128, 64 and so on down to 1. Two's complement changes one weight: the top bit weighs -128 (CS:APP 2.2.3). To read a number, add the weights of its 1 bits:</p>\n<p>$$-128x_7 + 64x_6 + \\cdots + 2x_1 + x_0$$</p>\n<table><tr><th>Bits</th><th>Unsigned</th><th>Two's complement</th></tr><tr><td><code>00010010</code></td><td>18</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td><code>11010010</code></td><td>210</td><td>-46</td></tr></table>\n<h2>Questions</h2>\n<section id='Q1'><p><b>Q1.</b> Any pattern that starts with 1, like <code>10110100</code>, is negative. Why?</p></section>\n<h2>Guess for next time (not graded)</h2>\n<section id='G'><p><code>00000110</code> is 6. Which steps turn it into the bits of -6?</p></section>"
  }
 },
 {
  "op": "set",
  "collection": "lessons/02/questions",
  "doc_id": "Q1",
  "data": {
   "id": "Q1",
   "type": "text",
   "redo": false,
   "hints": [],
   "options": [],
   "feedback": [
    {
     "attempt": 1,
     "answer": "the top bit is -128 and the rest add up to at most 127",
     "text": "64 + 32 + ... + 1 is 127, so with the top bit's -128 the sum stays below 0. You put it as \"the rest add up to at most 127\" (CS:APP 2.2.3)."
    }
   ]
  }
 },
